.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-set - Set this machine's Inbox directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox set <directory> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the directory received files are written to. Give a full path on this computer, written
the way this computer writes paths; ~ at the start means your home directory. A relative path is
refused. The directory is created if it does not exist and must be writable only by you.
Files already delivered stay where they are.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox set ~/Inbox
  pb inbox set /srv/incoming --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
